192-v3 trained 1,250 steps of 32 rows (0.51 epoch of 78,952 rows) in **4,400 s on a Modal A100-40GB**, peaking at 11 GB of memory ([v3 training summary](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/training/lfm3vl2b_v3/train_summary.json)). With AndroidControl and development evaluations added, one v3-sized cycle takes about 1.5 GPU-hours, most of the ~2.5 G4-hours left on Colab. With $18.44 already spent on Modal this month, roughly one more run remains there if the earlier $26–28 ceiling still applies; treat that as unconfirmed. Emulator hours are free but slow, and they are the real constraint on fair evaluation. The plan below keeps hyperparameters, image budget and harness fixed for the training run, so that any change in AW can be attributed to data. Under the project's preflight rule, every paid step first runs end-to-end on a tiny limit, upload included.
