209-Four smaller changes ride along. The final steps of answer episodes get a brief "seen: … / progress: …" thought stating the fact being reported, so the history carries it forward; this is the small-model form of GUI-Owl's memory-and-progress thoughts, and restricting it to answer episodes keeps teacher cost and decode latency low. Completion boundaries become explicit: question goals never end in `complete`, and action goals end in `complete` only on the gold final screen. The device's installed-app list goes into the prompt in training (the episode's app plus realistic distractors) and at inference to fix "Marker", with the same list given to GUI-Owl. No-change recovery rows, built from our own AndroidControl rows the GUI-Reflection way ([GUI-Reflection](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.08012)), go in at VeriGUI's 30% share only if v3's finished run shows loop counts near v2's rather than v1's, since a smaller share did nothing.
210-
211:The second run depends on what step 3 reveals. If answers are emitted but mis-formatted, or the model answers on action goals, spend it on a corrected v4.1. If failures look like compounding errors, spend it on the earlier plan's on-policy correction round: roll v4 through about 1,500 AndroidControl and GUI-Odyssey train episodes on the Mac with its own history, and record first-divergence states with the gold label. At 7B, training on own-history states moved AW from 21.7 to 34.0 ([UI-S1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.11543)), and keeping learner errors in the history beat pure expert distillation, 48.3 to 44.8 ([OpenMobile](https://arxiv.org/html/2604.15093)). Offline GRPO waits for a confirmed Modal budget and a pipeline that has already run end-to-end. Equally clear is what not to do: add more static human demonstrations, add history screenshots for parity, merge adapters, change the step budget or headline pass@k, fold harness tricks into model claims, or train the headline model on AW-app synthetic sets.
